section Merge_StairDivLoanTopGeneric_at_QTop

/-!
# Generic run facts for the division-endpoint loan window (LT15)

* `run_basis_xOnly`: a wire targeted only by `X` gates ends flipped by the
  parity of those gates (any state, any record).
* `run_basis_untouched`, `run_basis_endsCleared`: untouched wires keep their
  value; a wire whose last write is a measurement ends at `false`.
* `run_basis_records`: the basis part of a run never depends on the record.
* `run_shift`: a global phase flip commutes with `run`.
* `tapeFree_middle`: if `A ++ (B ++ C)` is record-independent from `s`, then
  `B` is record-independent from every state `run A a s`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace ECDSAAdd.Entrant.StairDivLoanTop

open ECDSAAdd












theorem run_basis_records : ∀ (P : Program) (m n : List Bool) (s t : State),
    s.basis = t.basis → (run P m s).basis = (run P n t).basis := by
  intro P
  induction P with
  | nil => intro m n s t h; exact h
  | cons i P ih =>
      intro m n s t h
      cases i with
      | X q => simp only [run]; apply ih; simp [h]
      | CX c q => simp only [run]; apply ih; simp [h]
      | CCX a1 a2 q => simp only [run]; apply ih; simp [h]
      | measureX q c0 c1 => simp only [run]; apply ih; simp [measureAndCorrect, h]










/-! ## K1 (replay budget): operand lists and bit masks for static program checks

`decide (q ∉ Instr.wires i)` builds a `Finset` per instruction (and per wire `q`); the checks
below test list operands once per instruction and wire sets as one bit mask per program. -/


















