section Merge_StairPhysicalInventory_at_QTop

/-!
# Physical omission inventory of the staircase

`place` is the literal outer placement of a field-tail label
(`StairOuterPlacement.outerPlace`).  This module decides which of the 68
canonical omission candidates `StairSchedule.retiredSites` can really be
omitted from the final 1,601-site record arena.

* The last 44 candidates, `base 720 .. base 764` without `base 760`, are
  exactly the last 44 retired roles.  Every record packet placement
  (`Placement5.pi j`), the late-sign map `OB5.sig 511`, and the field
  renames fix them, and their physical images are 44 distinct arena sites
  disjoint from the 15 old omissions and from the I/O wires.
  `final_qubits_le_1542` is the resulting inventory theorem.
* The first 24 candidates, `base 693 .. base 716`, are not arena sites at
  all (`retiredSites_low_outside`); the record already omits them.
* The corresponding 24 retired roles cannot supply replacements: role
  `base 719` is already an old omission (`role719_oldHole`), and the 23
  roles `base 696 .. base 718` are `Placement5` work labels that the record
  hosts on packet holes.  For example role `base 696` lives on
  `Rolling1588.s 90 4`, the C3 hole of packet 90, which the staircase's own
  packet-90 group still uses (`role696_shares_s454`,
  `s454_used_by_packet90`).  These sites therefore cannot be omitted.
-/

